-- story: A resize that changes its own frame
-- group: 3. Moving and resizing
-- status: needs-work
-- try: The pale rect is the page, and it fills the view because the view box reads the same
--   pageWidth and pageHeight. Drag a corner of it on the canvas. It moves, but it will not resize.
-- note: Resizing the page rect would change the view box by the same amount, so the whole view
--   rescales and the page still fills it. That is also why editing pageWidth by hand seems to do
--   nothing to the page while the circle changes size. The edge could never follow the pointer, so
--   the canvas refuses. The properties pane can still change the width. The fix is a gizmo that
--   draws both the box that was asked for and the box that resulted.
module Story exposing (..)

import KnottyDrawings exposing (..)
import Types exposing (..)

pageWidth :: Float
pageWidth = 240

pageHeight :: Float
pageHeight = 160

program = svg 480 320
    [ rect 0 0 pageWidth pageHeight |> set_fill alice_blue
    , circle 120 80 30 |> set_fill tomato
    ]
    |> set_view_box 0 0 pageWidth pageHeight
